# GW unofficial footer

Cite [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) Sec 10 and [`templates/Footer_Template_Gw_Print.md`](../../templates/Footer_Template_Gw_Print.md). **AGENTS.md wins.**

## Required on print HTML (`games/**/print/`, cheat sheets, datacard HTML)

- **Page 1:** `.gw-ip-banner` — word **UNOFFICIAL** prominent (cover equivalent).
- **Every page:** `.gw-ip-footer` — include *completely unofficial and in no way endorsed by Games Workshop Limited*; personal / no-charge / never for sale; short TM line; house copyright line; no GW logos.
- **Datacards:** micro footer D in `.ft` — UNOFFICIAL · not endorsed · personal use · © GW.
- CSS/HTML fragments: [`templates/Gw_Print_Banner.html`](../../templates/Gw_Print_Banner.html).

## Required on player-facing markdown (not `units/research/`)

- `## Games Workshop notice` **before** `## Change Log` (or one Attribution bullet) — same meaning as footer A; 40K vs KT copyright line.

## Export / PDF policy

- Event PDFs: **teaching paraphrase** + banner/footer. Do not export quote appendices as share packs unless the owner explicitly gates it.
- Never redistribute WarCom/GW downloadable PDFs (`eng_*`); pointers only.
- Scoped in-repo quotes stay under AGENTS Sec 10 paths only.

